000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, JULY 19, 2006\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:00 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer and Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 7:01 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r \r1. Real property negotiations, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.8\r Agency Negotiator: Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director\r Negotiating parties: City of Calabasas and Spotlight the Arts\r Instruction: Discussion regarding Office of State Library Construction title impact to property. \r Identity of property: Assessor�s Parcel Numbers 2068-003-900; 2068-003-901\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:30 p.m. from closed session and Mayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:42 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer and Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Ball, Bartlett, Colantuono, Coroalles, Lindamood, Parker, Rubin, Starns, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Mr. & Mrs. Antipolis. \r\rMichael Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that the Council added an item to the agenda entitled Smith vs. City of Calabasas for the approval of a settlement. He also stated that the Council did not take any action on the Closed Session which required reporting. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\rAlvia Saxs spoke regarding the proposed Spotlight the Arts project. Steven Summers spoke regarding arts and culture in the city. Don Schmitz thanked the Council regarding the Calabasas Highlands item on the previous agenda. \r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the July 5, 2006 City Council meeting. \r \r Recommendation from the Parks, Recreation and Education Commission to award Community Service Grants for the first funding cycle of FY 06/07 as identified in the staff report. \r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2006-227, amending Chapter 15.16 of Title 15 of the Calabasas Municipal Code, Flood Hazard Prevention. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1037, amending the ICMA Deferred Compensation Plan to permit loans. \r\r Recommendation to appropriate $60,000 of Air Quality Management District Subvention Funds to purchase two hybrid City vehicles. \r\r Recommendation to approve the addition of student representatives to the Agoura Hills/Calabasas Community Center Joint Powers Authority. \r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to approve Items #1, 3, 4, 5 and 6 with Councilmember Maurer�s ABSTENTION on Item #1. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rFollowing discussion, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve Consent Item #2. MOTION CARRIED 4/0/1 with Mayor Washburn�s ABSTENTION.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING #1 \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1038, requesting a Conditional Use Permit, Site Plan, and Tentative Tract Map to construct a 60 unit Senior Condominium development for property located at 26705 Malibu Hills Road (APN: 2064-004-051) within the CB (Commercial-Business Park) Zoning District.\r\rMayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\rGeoff Starns, Senior Planner, provided the staff report.\r\rSteve Kaplan, applicant for the project, discussed issues related to the project. Matthew Doss spoke in support of the project. Dale Reicheneder, President, Steeplechase Homeowners Association spoke of the HOA�s concerns regarding the project.\r\rMayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to adopt Resolution No. 2006-1038, requesting a Conditional Use Permit, Site Plan, and Tentative Tract Map to construct a 60 unit Senior Condominium development for property located at 26705 Malibu Hills Road. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rThe City Council recessed at 9:50 p.m. and reconvened at 10:03 p.m.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING #2 \r\r Hold a public hearing with respect to the Fiscal Year 2006-07 levy of assessments in connection with the Landscape Maintenance Districts and the proposed increase of assessments in certain zones thereof; and, following tabulation of mail ballots, adopt Resolution No. 2006-1033, certifying the results of the assessment ballot proceeding with respect to the proposed increase and �Resolution No. 2006-1034, confirming a diagram and assessment for the Landscape Maintenance Districts for Fiscal Year 2006-07.\r\rMayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\rDebby Cobb, Consultant, provided the staff report and reported the results of the tabulation of mail ballots.\r\rMayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\r\r\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, Resolution No. 2006-1033, certifying the results of the assessment ballot proceeding; and �adopt Resolution No. 2006-1034, confirming a diagram and assessment for the Landscape Maintenance Districts for Fiscal Year 2006-07. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r\r Discussion regarding postal service issues and potential adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1035, requesting Congressman Henry Waxman to appeal the decision by the United States Postal Service to deny the request for a ZIP Code boundary change in the 91301/91302 area.\r\rJeff Scott, Calabasas, Pat Clark, Calabasas, Brian Oppenheim, Calabasas, Candice Weber, Calabasas, Dale Reicheneder, Robbie Amodio, Calabasas, Mary Gehret, Calabasas, Clark Canfield, Calabasas, Priscilla Lee, Calabasas, Robert Lia, Calabasas, Norman Buehring, Calabasas, Gary Rogovin, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the item. Melissa Olen, Calabasas, Lauren Engel, Calabasas, Nick Omana, Calabasas, Christopher Sutton, Calabasas, Joanne Siracusano, Calabasas, spoke in support of changing the zip code.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to instruct the City Attorney to preserve the appeal. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rMayor Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to continue the item to the 2nd meeting in September. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1036, setting forth policies and procedures for commission meetings. \r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to adopt Resolution No. 2006-1036, setting forth policies and procedures for commission meetings. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of June 24, 2006 to July 7, 2006. \r\r No Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Mayor Washburn provided an update on the Headwaters Corners Mountains Restoration Trust Task Force. He provided an update on the bid for the Civic Center project.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles stated that there was nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested that an item regarding affordable housing be placed on a future agenda.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 11:43 p.m.\r\r\r____________________________________ \rGwen Peirce, Assistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r07/19/06\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r07/19/06\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000